Explanation of the change:

- We eliminate the old “symmetric adjustment” block that frequently hit a `Math.floor(…)=0` and effectively collapsed the bounds to `NaN`, preventing any rendering.
- Instead, we simply guarantee that whenever your data crosses zero, the computed bounds will encompass 0.  That is enough to allow bar charts (and any other chart type) to draw correctly when you have negative values.
